{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A lamb for each father's house</b> The reason for this commandment is that the constellation Aries (the lamb) is in its full power in the month of Nisan, for it is the constellation of growth; therefore He commanded to slaughter a lamb and eat it, to make known that it was not by the power of a constellation that we went forth from there, but by the decree of the Most High. And according to the opinion of our Sages, that the Egyptians worshipped it (Exodus Rabbah 16:2), all the more so did He make known through this commandment that He humiliated their gods and their power, it being in its supreme position. Thus they said (ibid.): \"Take for yourselves sheep and slaughter\" — the gods of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The citation שמו\"ר (Shemot Rabbah) is expanded as Exodus Rabbah 16:2, following standard reference conventions; the final quotation is a midrashic paraphrase of the verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:55.945120668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}